<section class="best-worlds-stage" aria-labelledby="best-worlds-heading" aria-describedby="best-worlds-description">
  <h2 id="best-worlds-heading" class="sr-only">
    The flexibility of model reasoning and the consistency of formal program analysis combined
  </h2>
  <p id="best-worlds-description" class="sr-only">
    OpenTaint discovers application-specific vulnerability patterns, turns them into readable formal specifications, and enforces them with repeatable whole-project analysis on every code change.
  </p>

  <div class="best-worlds-inner">
    <div class="best-worlds-visual">
      <div class="best-worlds-toolbar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span><i></i> OPEN SOURCE, BATTERIES INCLUDED</span>
        <span>DISCOVER → ENACT → SCAN → TRIAGE</span>
      </div>

      <svg class="best-worlds-flow" viewBox="0 0 1200 560" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="best-worlds-flow-muted" d="M374 294 H434 M766 294 H826" />
        <path class="best-worlds-flow-active" d="M374 294 H434 M766 294 H826" />
      </svg>
      <span class="best-worlds-flow-label best-worlds-flow-label-left" aria-hidden="true">ENACT</span>
      <span class="best-worlds-flow-label best-worlds-flow-label-right" aria-hidden="true">SCAN</span>

      <article class="best-worlds-side best-worlds-reasoning">
        <header class="best-worlds-side-heading">
          <small>AGENTIC / DISCOVER</small>
          <h3>The flexibility of <strong>model reasoning</strong></h3>
        </header>

        <p class="best-worlds-outcome best-worlds-reasoning-outcome">
          Adapts security knowledge to your application
        </p>

        <div class="best-worlds-values" aria-label="Values of model reasoning">
          <div><i>01</i><span><b>INTERPRETS INTENT</b><small>Routes, framework conventions, and trust boundaries</small></span></div>
          <div><i>02</i><span><b>FINDS APP-SPECIFIC RISK</b><small>Unique sources, sinks, and data transformations</small></span></div>
          <div><i>03</i><span><b>LEARNS FROM REVIEW</b><small>Each discovery becomes reusable security knowledge</small></span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="reasoning-inference">
          <span>PROJECT-SPECIFIC SSTI PATTERN</span>
          <p>Spring request data reaches the <code>template engine</code></p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="best-worlds-core">
        <header>
          <span>LEAN / ENACT</span>
          <strong>CODE TO FORMAL SPECIFICATION</strong>
          <i>Related code becomes reusable security knowledge</i>
        </header>

        <div class="best-worlds-code-map">
          <section class="best-worlds-code-panel best-worlds-application-code" aria-label="Spring application code with the taint source, transformation, and sink highlighted">
            <header><span>SPRING APPLICATION CODE</span><i>PreviewController.java</i></header>
            <pre><code><span>@PostMapping("/preview")</span>
<span>String preview(HttpServletRequest req) {</span>
<span class="code-line-source">  var data = req.getParameter(</span>
<span class="code-line-source">      "template");</span>
<span class="code-line-transform">  var view = data.strip();</span>
<span class="code-line-soft">  audit("preview_requested");</span>
<span class="code-line-sink">  return engine.process(view,</span>
<span class="code-line-sink">      context);</span>
<span>}</span></code></pre>
          </section>

          <div class="best-worlds-code-key">
            <strong><span>$DATA</span> → <span>$TAINTED</span></strong>
            <b>METAVARIABLES ARE DATA TAINT MARKS</b>
          </div>

          <section class="best-worlds-code-panel best-worlds-formal-code" aria-label="Formal SSTI specification expressed with metavariables">
            <header><span>FORMAL SPECIFICATION</span><i>security/ssti.yml</i></header>
            <pre><code><span><em>- pattern:</em> |</span>
<span>    <b class="code-meta-data">$DATA</b> = <b class="code-meta-source">$REQ</b>.getParameter(...);</span>
<span class="code-line-ellipsis">    ...</span>
<span>    <b class="code-meta-data">$TAINTED</b> = <b class="code-meta-data">$DATA</b>.strip();</span>
<span class="code-line-ellipsis">    ...</span>
<span>    <b class="code-meta-sink">$ENGINE</b>.process(<b class="code-meta-data">$TAINTED</b>, ...);</span></code></pre>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="best-worlds-side best-worlds-analysis">
        <header class="best-worlds-side-heading">
          <small>CONTINUOUS / SCAN</small>
          <h3>The consistency of <strong>formal program analysis</strong></h3>
        </header>

        <p class="best-worlds-outcome best-worlds-analysis-outcome">
          <strong>One rule. Every path. Every change.</strong>
          <span>The same security decision across the whole project.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="analysis-path" aria-label="A formally analyzed source-to-sink path">
